# Axis: failure direction on absent machinery
COUNT: 82 findings
DEPENDENT: 82 / STATED: 25
## Findings
1. Structure beats Willpower — standards-coverage CI ratchet — “the build fails when…coverage falls below its committed floor” — SILENT when the workflow/ratchet itself is absent; constitutional enforcement needs fail-closed release/build behavior.
2. Self-Hosting — Standards-Conformance Gate and `/spec-converge` reviewer — “mandatory step; a run that skips it without a stated unavailability reason fails report validation” — SILENT after unavailability is merely stated; canonical changes need fail closed, while advisory dogfood review may fail open.
3. The Body and the Mind — tier classifier, LLM-supervised gates, decision audit trails — “every decision of consequence is made by the mind, informed by the body, and recorded” — SILENT if the model or recorder is absent; consequential action needs fail closed, ordinary user communication needs a bounded fail-open path.
4. Structure Decides Alone Only on an Exact Match — `MessageSentinel` exact-match floor plus model — “with no model reachable, structure’s coverage is exactly the enumerated list and nothing more” — STATED mixed direction: exact matches fail closed to STOP; non-listed stops fail open — honest and bounded, but unsafe for paraphrased emergency stops.
5. Deferral = Deletion — deferral-referent CI lint — “fails the build when a marker refers to nothing” — SILENT if the lint/CI does not run; shipping unresolved promises needs fail closed.
6. Close the Loop — beacons, maturation entries, periodic review jobs — “add one — a beacon, a maturation entry, a periodic review job” — SILENT if cadence machinery stops; closure claims should fail closed, while ongoing work should continue with a loud degraded-state record.
7. Observation Needs Structure — refused-without-it stores and transition gates — “Encode every observation duty as a refused-without-it field” — SILENT if the refusing store/gate is absent; state mutation should fail closed.
8. Intelligence Infers, Keywords Only Guard — model classifier and keyword lint — “Fail-OPEN: on any uncertainty (model down, breaker open, low confidence)…pass the message through” — STATED fail-open — safe for a message-consuming inbound gate because it protects operator reach.
9. Recall Over Our Own Material Is by Meaning, Not by Word-Match — route/mechanism lint — “refuses a route that reaches the literal matcher while being advertised with meaning-words” — SILENT if lint is missing; advertising semantic recall should fail closed, although literal search itself may remain available under an honest label.
10. Intelligent Prompts — An LLM Gate Must Not String-Match — prompt ratchet, rule registry, human review — “an unclassified or misclassified judgment-shaped rule fails closed” — STATED fail-closed for classification degradation — safe for content/action gates.
11. Quantitative Claims Must Bind a Subject — `time-claim` verifier and live clock — “Positive verification requires an explicit subject binding” — SILENT if the clock/verifier is unavailable; because this verifier can interrupt correct messages, unknown should fail open to pass-through.
12. The Operator Channel Is Sacred — `MessageSentinel`, capacity-shed path, circuit breaker — “The safe failure direction for inbound operator comms is DELIVERY” — STATED fail-open — correct for operator reach.
13. The Agent Is Always Reachable — reachability predicate, reserved spawn lane, drainer, breaker, watchdog — “the terminal state…is a SLOW heartbeat retry…NEVER ‘no session at all’” — STATED fail toward reachability — correct; safety remains bounded and degradation is surfaced.
14. Architectural Agency in the Gap — gates, audits, journals, identity files and grounding — “the gates, audits, journals, identity files, and grounding system are how the agent closes that gap” — SILENT if those mechanisms disappear; consequential autonomous action needs fail closed, with communication preserved.
15. A Wall Is a Hypothesis — `MessagingToneGate` B16 and spec reviewer — “an outbound message…is blocked unless a capability inventory is shown” — SILENT if the gate/model is unavailable; this protects autonomy rather than safety, so user delivery should fail open with the missing review logged.
16. Never a False Blocker — `MessagingToneGate` B17 and PreToolUse hook — “an outbound message…is held and handed back” — SILENT on machinery loss; fail open to communication, not fail closed into silence.
17. The Stop Reason Is the Work — autonomous-completion evaluator and B18 — “requires a derived-standard proposal, a built artifact, or a named operator-only residual before permitting…stop” — SILENT if evaluator/gate is absent; safe behavior is continuation, i.e. fail closed against stopping.
18. Self-Unblock Before Escalating — BlockerLedger, `SelfUnblockChecklist`, Tier-1 authority — “missing/ambiguous metadata fails CLOSED” — STATED fail-closed — correct for credentials, permissions and asserted blockers.
19. Distrust Temporary Success — autonomous-completion evaluator and reviewer — “a symptom-reset that recurs does NOT count as done” — SILENT if evaluation machinery is absent; completion claims should fail closed.
20. Remove What Demands Attention — duplicate-definition lint — “a matcher that parses zero articles fails loud rather than reporting clean” — SILENT if the lint/CI itself disappears; constitutional duplication checks need fail-closed builds.
21. Verify the State, Not Its Symbol — detectors, sentinels, gates and reviewers — “unknown must fail toward the least-harmful action for that specific detector” — STATED context-sensitive direction — correct: security unknown blocks; recovery/notice unknown stays quiet.
22. A Dispatch Supplies the Question and Withholds the Answer — dispatch lint and template migrator — “every templated reviewer dispatch must carry” the protocol — SILENT if lint/migration is unavailable; consequential delegated verdicts should not be accepted without the protocol, so fail closed at review.
23. Know Your Principal — identity registry, session binding and `PrincipalGuard` — “An unresolved principal halts and questions; it does not proceed” — STATED fail-closed — correct for identity and authority.
24. Framework-Agnostic — and Framework-Optimizing — capability registry, compiler exhaustiveness, CI and review gate — “Options a path can’t honor degrade to advisory hints, never hard failures” — STATED fail-open to another working path — correct because this protects reach and provider portability.
25. Cross-Machine Coherence — fenced lease, lease coordinator/transports and dedupe ledger — “Exactly one machine holds a VALID lease at a time” — SILENT if lease authority is unavailable; side effects should fail closed, while inbound delivery needs a non-mutating fail-open queue.
26. An Instar Agent Is Always a Multi-Machine Entity — machine-local lint and semantic reviewer — “The lint ships REPORT-FIRST (a non-blocking signal)” — SILENT on reviewer outage; the current effective direction is fail-open, but state-fragmenting exceptions should fail closed.
27. Cross-Store Coherence Is an Invariant — scheduled coherence audit and wiring-time validator — “refuses to ENABLE against a dependency store that cannot resolve the verified operator” — STATED fail-closed at wiring time — correct for identity/authority; loss of the scheduled audit itself remains unspecified.
28. Testing Integrity — test tiers, typed obligation profile and CI — “an unregistered or dynamically-discovered boundary must remain UNRESOLVED and fail closed” — STATED fail-closed, though not yet implemented — correct for shipping unclassified significant/critical work.
29. Test Identity Never Enters Production State — write guards, registry validation and daily audit — “A write…into a real state store is refused structurally” — SILENT if guard and audit machinery are absent; production identity writes must fail closed.
30. Scrape/Parser Fixture Realness — fixture loader, realness lint and test suite — “the lint proves the named test exists + feeds-and-asserts” — SILENT if lint/CI is absent; parser shipping should fail closed.
31. Zero-Failure — pre-push hook, CI branch protection and session test-health gate — “a red suite blocks the push” — SILENT if those gates do not run; pushes/releases need fail closed.
32. LLM-Supervised Execution — Tier-1 LLM supervisor — “Every critical pipeline has…a Tier-1 LLM supervisor” — SILENT if the supervisor/model is unavailable; critical pipelines need fail closed or a declared deterministic safe rung.
33. Observability — metrics ledger and operator surfaces — “Every feature ships with metrics” — SILENT if metrics machinery is absent; safety-critical features should fail closed at activation, ordinary features may fail open only with loud degradation.
34. Expected Capacity Enforcement Is an Outcome, Not a Degradation — capacity contract, typed result, lint and restart test — “Every bounded writer registers a versioned contract” — SILENT if contract/lint/runtime accounting is missing; bounded writes should fail closed at the budget.
35. Observable Intelligence — single provider funnel, metrics ledger and lint — “Every LLM call…must be recorded” — SILENT if the ledger/funnel is unavailable. Because this protects accountability, autonomous LLM action should fail closed. Its pending status instead prevents builds from failing solely on it, effectively fail-open and unsafe.
36. A Refusal Stays a Refusal — typed routing result, receiver trace, loss notice and canary — “The refusing side writes a trace…before the refusing function returns” — SILENT if trace/notice machinery is unavailable; rejection must remain fail closed against success-mapping, with an alternate loud user notice.
37. Runtime End-to-End Proof — scheduled delivery canary and alert path — “a synthetic probe exercises the full real path on a cadence” — SILENT if the canary job itself stops; delivery must continue, but monitoring failure should fail loud through an independent path.
38. Migration Parity — `PostUpdateMigrator` and migration-guarantee test — “the binding gate…runs eight committed pre-migration agent shapes” — SILENT if migrator/gate is missing; release/update should fail closed.
39. Migration-Consumer Completeness — migration registry and blocking lint — “every declared producer, consumer, and validator must acknowledge that revision” — SILENT if lint/CI is absent; canonical migrations need fail closed.
40. Canonical Pipeline Operational Completeness — manifest lint, cadence jobs and runtime positive control — “Accepted-intake routes and jobs carry typed…metadata” — SILENT when owner/cadence machinery dies; admission should fail closed rather than accept work that cannot drain.
41. Compaction Parity — recovery hook, migrator and parity test — “every `*/session-context` fetch…must appear in the compaction-recovery hook” — SILENT if recovery/migration machinery is absent; consequential action should fail closed, while the user channel should remain reachable through a fresh-session fallback.
42. Tiered Development — tier classifier, precommit gate and audit cadence — “the development gate computes a tier signal…and the agent declares” — SILENT if classifier/audit machinery is unavailable; unresolved risk should take the stricter path.
43. Constitutional Traceability — Standards-Conformance Gate and LLM reviewer — “the SEMANTIC layer…DOES fail open when the reviewer is degraded or unreachable” — STATED fail-open — unsafe for constitutional shipping because this is not a user-reach gate. It also makes unreviewed weak fits indistinguishable after shipment.
44. Friction Is a Spec — lessons-aware reviewer prompt — “nothing beyond a reviewer prompt carries this standard” — SILENT if reviewer is unavailable; fail-open is proportionate, but the degradation should be recorded rather than mistaken for enforcement.
45. Notice + Solve Inefficiencies — reminder/reviewer machinery — “a reminder is not a gate” — SILENT; fail-open is proportionate because this is improvement discovery, not safety, but missed coverage should remain observable.
46. Bounded Notification Surface — topic-creation ceiling, attention guard, funnel lint and burst test — “the build fails if more than the budget of topics get created” — SILENT if runtime funnel or CI is absent; automatic topic creation must fail closed while existing-topic delivery remains open.
47. Notices Route to the Alerts Topic — attention-routing chokepoint and topic budget — “routes every item into the…hub unless…legacy opt-out” — SILENT if the hub/routing machinery is unavailable; fail closed on creating a new topic, not on delivering to an existing conversation.
48. Conservative Outbound — outbound-emitter lint and disposition reviewer — “New emitters ship silent-by-default and opt IN” — SILENT if lint/reviewer is absent; proactive outbound should fail closed, while direct requested replies must remain deliverable.
49. No Unbounded Loops — backoff, breaker, cap and sustained-failure tests — “after sustained failure it stops attempting and surfaces the degradation once” — STATED fail-closed on repetition, with a bounded slow-retry exception for eternal sentinels — safe.
50. Keep the Doorway/Model Map Current — scheduled scan job and freshness lint — “a machine whose scan silently stops looks identical to one whose map is current” — STATED current fail-open/silent gap, with eventual fail-loud freshness lint — unsafe as stated; runtime should retain the last known route for reach, but scan loss must be detected independently.
51. Judgment Within Floors — LLM arbiter and deterministic fallback ladder — “fallback…always ends at a deterministic rung” — STATED deterministic conservative fallback — safe for consequential judgment.
52. Decision Provenance & Outcome Review — provenance log and graded-review job — “Every LLM judgment call durably logs” its context and decision — SILENT if logger/job is unavailable; autonomous judgment should fail closed when accountability cannot be recorded.
53. Stall Coverage Is Enumerated, Not Discovered — matrix validator, CI ratchet, codemod and live-check job — “a missing file is a red build, not a silent pass” — SILENT if validator/CI/live-check machinery is absent; onboarding should fail closed.
54. Bounded Blast Radius — host spawn semaphore, spawn-provider funnel, lint and burst test — “A capacity shed of a gating call fails CLOSED (hold)” — STATED fail-closed — safe for physical-host protection, but conflicts with the user-path rule below unless the priority/reserved-lane exception is explicit here.
55. Capacity Safety — controller registry, convergence test, forcing lint and class-closure gate — “fail-closed” lint, but “report-only under…`dryRun`” and no universal funnel — STATED mixed direction — unsafe for physical safety because an unregistered/obfuscated self-action can fail open.
56. Live-User-Channel Proof Before Done — live-test harness and completion gate — “Failure direction: fail CLOSED toward user-facing” — STATED fail-closed — correct for shipping user-visible behavior without evidence.
57. Ownership-Gated Side Effects — `SpawnAdmission` and ownership E2E proof — “ownership-resolution error fails toward action loudly and boundedly” — STATED fail-open toward action — wrong for session creation, rebinding and side effects; unknown ownership must fail closed to local mutation while forwarding/queuing remains available.
58. Autonomous Throughput Floor — read breaker and authenticated status surface — “It never notifies, dispatches, remediates, or creates attention” — SILENT if monitoring disappears; fail-open/no-action is safe, but loss of the observer should be visible independently.
59. Iterative Audit to Convergence — convergence writer, precommit gate and CI ratchet — “refuses the stamp unless ≥2 rounds ended with a zeroed…final round” — SILENT if the writer/gates are absent; convergence claims should fail closed.
60. A Decision That Can Block Must Live Where the Checks Can See It — blocking-decision lint — “refuses an undeclared file in the population” — SILENT if lint/CI is missing; introducing blocking decisions should fail closed.
61. No Silent Degradation to Brittle Fallback — shared intelligence router and LLM gate ratchet — “must SWAP PROVIDER…or FAIL CLOSED” — STATED fail-closed — correct for safety/content gates, but directly conflicts with the outbound tone-gate direction in Finding 71.
62. An Autonomous Run Must Outlive Its Session — resume queue, drainer, host lock and guard-posture probe — “fail-closed on any uncertainty” and a disabled queue raises an alert — STATED fail-closed plus loud degradation — safe for shared-volume conflict, provided the alert path remains independent.
63. One Failure Teaches Every Guard — enforcement-gap/fingerprint lints — “fails the build on a malformed gap [or] stale sweep” — SILENT if the lints/CI are absent; constitutional enforcement records need fail closed.
64. Bug-Fix Evidence Bar — Side-Effects Review Gate as its validator — “Never claim something is fixed…until the original failure has been reproduced” — SILENT if the validating gate/reviewer is unavailable; ship/fixed claims need fail closed.
65. No Deferrals — precommit orphan-deferral gate — “the commit is refused otherwise (the override is an env var)” — SILENT on hook absence, and the override is an explicit bypass without an outage policy; shipping should fail closed.
66. Maturation Path — maturation-plan convergence gate — “REFUSES the convergence stamp” — SILENT if the chokepoint is absent; staged features need fail-closed graduation.
67. A Dark Feature Guards Nothing — guard inventory, posture view and alert probe — “dark-but-load-bearing…ALERTS” — SILENT if classification/probe machinery is down; load-bearing dependence should fail closed or carry an expiring, loud operator acceptance.
68. Side-Effects Review Gate — precommit hook and artifact validator — “refuses the commit when the side-effects artifact is not staged” — SILENT if hook/gate is unavailable; shipping needs fail closed.
69. Token-Audit Completeness — attribution lint, usage-contract test and metrics — “Every LLM-calling feature must carry `attribution.component`” — SILENT if audit machinery is absent; activation should fail closed for unaccountable LLM calls.
70. User-Facing Fixes Ship Live — production judgment, audit log and off-switch — “bake the judgment in production (fail-open, audit logs, per-agent off-switch)” — STATED bounded fail-open — appropriate for user-visible fixes only when classification is undisputed and rollback remains live.
71. The User Experience Is the Product — UX-liveness watchdog, inbound queue, tone gate and resource priority lane — “check-unavailable [must] fail toward the user” while “content-unsafe [must] fail closed” — STATED split direction — correct for reach, but conflicts with Finding 61’s universal fail-closed LLM-gate rule and Finding 54’s universal capacity-shed hold.
72. Mobile-Complete Operator Actions — dashboard/link surfaces and side-effects reviewer — “the side-effects review…asks explicitly” whether actions are phone-completable — SILENT if review/dashboard/tunnel machinery is unavailable; operator-required rollout should fail closed.
73. Operator-Surface Quality — precommit operator-surface assertion and outbound raw-text detector — “a ‘no’ or an unjustified ‘n/a’ blocks the commit” — SILENT if gate/detector is absent; operator-surface changes should fail closed.
74. Dashboard UX Standard — CI-enforced dashboard floors — “each floor is a machine-checkable test that fails the build” — SILENT if CI/tests do not run; dashboard changes should fail closed.
75. Agent Proposes, Operator Approves — operator-surface assertion, request store and server renderer — “the authority statement…must be authored by the server” — SILENT if renderer/assertion is unavailable; authorization execution must fail closed and surface an unavailable approval.
76. The Agent Carries the Loop — commitment tracker, beacon, reconciler, staleness governor and tone gate — “missing/false suppresses every…user send while internal cadence…continues” — STATED fail-closed for outbound notification — safe for anti-nagging, but failure of the internal follow-through machinery itself is unspecified and should fail loud.
77. Agent Awareness — capability index and discoverability lint — “refuses a route that is neither surfaced…nor explicitly allowlisted” — SILENT if lint/index machinery is unavailable; feature/route shipping should fail closed.
78. Never-Waste Feedback — automatic correction detector and `HumanAsDetectorLog` — “built-in infrastructure detects it [and] ingests it” — SILENT if detector/log is unavailable; interaction should fail open, but capture loss must be loud and durably queued.
79. Signal vs. Authority — low-context detector plus intelligent blocking gate — “Only a higher-level, full-context intelligent gate has blocking authority” — SILENT if that intelligent gate is unavailable; the article needs the same content-sensitive split as Findings 8, 61 and 71.
80. Near-Silent Notifications — watchers, audit log and notification routing — “the audit log is the record” — SILENT if audit/routing machinery fails; routine outbound should fail closed, but terminal user-affecting failure must use an alternate loud path.
81. Self-Heal Before Notify — watchers, healers, schema lint, reviewer and side-effects gate — “only the exhausted-heal path reaches the operator,” while the lint is “REPORT-FIRST” — STATED mixed direction — runtime escalation is safe, but nonblocking enforcement can allow a first-notify watcher to ship and is unsafe for outbound attention.
82. Truthful Provenance — attributed message carrier and separate internal/user channels — “these are structurally distinct channels” — SILENT if attribution is absent; unverified input must fail closed against being treated as the user, while remaining visible as untrusted/system input.

The sharp same-machinery conflict is the outbound `MessagingToneGate`/LLM-gating path: **No Silent Degradation to Brittle Fallback** requires provider failure to swap or fail closed, while **The User Experience Is the Product** requires that same unavailable tone gate to use a deterministic floor and send clean messages. A second conflict exists at scarce spawn capacity: **Bounded Blast Radius** says a shed gating call holds, while the UX article says the user-facing path must preempt background work and fail toward response. These can be reconciled only by explicitly scoping the fail-closed rules away from inbound/user-reach chokepoints and naming the reserved deterministic path in every governing article.

## Articles reviewed
89